From 3b71ebd9e920ef0060400b4757f6bd3063f7c911 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:19:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): honor or note end_units across mill posts and gate
 UI offer

Add the top-level `endUnits` post manifest contract (`"<inch> <mm>"`,
`"note"`, or absent) so every post handles `postOptions.EndUnits`
consistently:
- `fanuc.cps`, `mazak.cps`, `doosan-dnm.cps` (`"G20 G21"`) and
  `sinumerik.cps` (`"G700 G710"`) emit the requested unit word right
  before `M30` / `M2` after the final retract when differing from the
  program unit (`tormach`, `grblhal`, `tinyg` declare `"G20 G21"`).
- `haas.cps`, `carvera.cps`, and `heidenhain.cps` declare `"note"` and
  emit a one-time `END UNITS NOT WRITTEN ...` note via `note()` when
  asked for an incompatible/switch end unit.
- `camcraft_post::post::end_units` refuses undeclared scripts by name
  before any hook runs when `EndUnits` is set.
- `posting::end_units_words` drives the Post dialog and `Setup -> Post`
  picker so only posts declaring unit words offer the combo (labeled
  with those words), while carried-over non-`Leave` values on unsupported
  posts get a one-click reset.

Fixes #2189

Co-Authored-By: Antigravity <noreply@anthropic.com>
